"use strict";

/* generated from story/scenes/act4_ch21.md — do not edit */

Object.assign(ENEMIES,{
 reelkeeper:{name:"Reel-Keeper of the Outer Lock",hp:38,p2at:14,
  open:"The checkpoint officer sets down your forged waybill, aligns it with the desk's edge, and stands \u2014 a broad, unhurried woman whose qi is wound on her arms in neat white skeins. \u201CThe hand is good,\u201D she says. \u201CThe ink is wrong. Mulberry-soot, downriver press. We mill our own. Hold still, merchant; inventory resists, people explain.\u201D",
  p2text:"She stops conserving herself. The skeins on her arms pay out all at once, and the little lock-house fills with white.",
  moves:[{n:"Keeper's Bracing",kind:"stance",st:"iron",text:"She squares her stance, qi setting on her shoulders in lacquered coats.",tele:"She is bracing \u2014 lacquer-iron settling coat on coat."},
   {n:"Skein-lash",d:5,drain:1},
   {n:"Winding the reel",kind:"charge",text:"Both arms cross; the white skeins begin to wind tight, humming.",tele:"The skeins are winding \u2014 the cast comes next."},
   {n:"Cast the net",d:11,kind:"release"}],
  p2:[{n:"Paying out",kind:"stance",st:"flow",text:"The skeins run loose and she moves like thrown silk.",tele:"The skeins run slack \u2014 thrown-silk speed, nothing braced."},
   {n:"Skein-lash, doubled",d:7,drain:1},
   {n:"Cast the net",d:9}]}});


SC["a4c21_guest"]={t:()=>P(`The white boat is exactly on time, and the courtesy begins at the gangplank and never once stops.`)+P(`Madam Xian receives your whole company as if hosting were the boat's cargo: your preferred tea, Ruan's preferred silence, a stove-side seat angled for an old woman's bones before anyone asks. For three days upriver she answers every question you put to her, fully, accurately, and with evident pleasure, which you have long since learned is the Court's most efficient way of hiding things: under more truth than you can carry.`)+((G.f.a3_marked=="sho")?(P(`She and Granny Sho conduct a three-day war of perfect manners that neither acknowledges. On the second evening Sho holds out her cup, and Madam Xian fills it, and the white thread on the old woman's shoulder lies flat as paint the whole time. “Your surety travels well,” Madam Xian observes. “Your sister sleeps badly the week before a reunion. We have that from forty years of records.” The cup does not so much as tremble. That, you think, is what forty years of sweeping buys.`)):(P(`She and Ruan negotiate nothing for three days in the language of seating arrangements and poured tea, and the white thread on his shoulder lies flat as paint through all of it. Once, passing, she says: “Your surety keeps admirable books, weaver. The Court will enjoy auditing alongside him.” Ruan writes that down too.`)))+P(`On the third evening she says, conversationally: “Tomorrow, the Thousand Reels. A request, from the Lady herself: enter looking UP. First-time guests stare at the water-gates, and the gates are nothing. The city is the loom. It would grieve her if you missed it.”`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Dawn, and the upper lake opens like a held breath.`,go:"a4c21_city"}]};

SC["a4c21_spy"]={t:()=>P(`The tribute barge takes six days, and you spend them becoming Wen Duo, a silk-trade auditor with cargo interests, bad knees, and a northern accent borrowed from a bridge-keeper you once fixed a bridge for.`)+P(`Ruan's forgeries are art: waybills aged with tea, a chop carved from a boot-heel, marginalia in three hands. The network's last letter, decoded over the brazier, gives the procedure: the Outer Lock, where consignment paper meets the Court's own millwork, and one Reel-Keeper with a reputation for reading ink the way priests read entrails.`)+((G.f.a3_marked=="sho")?(P(`Granny Sho travels openly — the Court claimed her shoulder, so the Court can host her; she boarded the white boat at the Heron with the rest of the surety etiquette, and her last word to you on the dock was a dry one: “They'll watch me to find you. So I'll be VERY interesting. Mind your ink, boy.”`)):(P(`Ruan travels openly — claimed is claimed; the white boat took him aboard at the Heron with full surety honors, and his last word on the dock was bookkeeper-flat: “They will watch me to find you. So I will be tedious beyond human endurance. It's a gift. Mind your ink, brother.”`)))+P(`The Outer Lock at dusk: a white lock-house astride the channel, skeins of pale qi drying on racks like a fisherman's nets, and a broad unhurried officer who takes your waybill, reads it twice, and looks up with the mild interest of a woman finding an error in a sum.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Talk first — you've audited real tribute paper for a year, and you know what her ink objection is worth.`,req:()=>(G.insight>=13),rq:"(needs Insight 13)",do:()=>{addIns(1);note("+1 Insight. You concede the ink before she finishes \u2014 downriver press, mulberry-soot, a SAMPLE waybill, you explain, carried precisely because the mills differ, and would the Keeper prefer your principal's chop on Court stock? Ten minutes later she is showing you HER ledger's problem cases and you are diagnosing skims for her. She stamps you through with professional warmth. You are inside the Court's paper now, which is inside the Court.");},go:"a4c21_through"},
  {id:"c1",l:`The skeins on her arms are already moving. Let the waybill go and meet her.`,go:"a4c21_keeper"}]};

SC["a4c21_keeper"]={img:"court",
 combat:"reelkeeper",
 win:"a4c21_through",
 lose:"a4c21_caught",
 t:()=>""};

SC["a4c21_through"]={t:()=>((G.f.a4_route=="spy")?(P(`Past the Outer Lock, the channel runs between mulberry orchards in their first leaf, and barge traffic thickens around you: silk out, rice in, paper everywhere. Wen Duo's chop now carries a Keeper's stamp, which opens doors faster than gold. By the time the city rises out of the lake haze you are three introductions deep into the tribute trade's middle management, and you know the names of four men who schedule consignments and hate their work quietly.`)):("")),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`The Thousand Reels, from the water.`,go:"a4c21_city"}]};

SC["a4c21_caught"]={t:()=>P(`She winds you in white to the elbows, professionally, almost gently, and sits you down in her lock-house while she rewrites your paperwork in her own clean hand.`)+P(`“Wen Duo, of nowhere, auditor of nothing.” No anger in it at all. “A weaver, by the gold all over my checkpoint. You were on a LIST, merchant — the Lady keeps a page for you. Walking in under false ink doesn't void the invitation. It just changes your column.” She stamps the new sheet: CONSIGNMENT, VOLUNTARY SURRENDER PRESUMED, HANDLE AS GUEST-IN-BOND. “Congratulations. You are the politest cargo on this river.”`)+SYS(`The spy route has degraded to guest-in-bond: you enter the Court collected, not concealed. The deepest door opens — from the wrong side.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`They ship you upriver with the tribute.`,do:()=>{G.f.a4_route="prisoner";G.f.a4_caught=true;},go:"a4c21_prisoner"}]};

SC["a4c21_prisoner"]={t:()=>P(`The collection office at the lake's edge processes you with a tenderness that is worse than cruelty would be.`)+((!G.f.a4_caught)?(P(`You walked in. That's what none of their forms have a box for: a weaver, THE weaver, presenting himself at the consignment desk like a man paying a tax. The clerk reads your name, goes very still, sends for three superiors in ascending order of silk quality, and the last one — a Reel-Mistress with kind exhausted eyes — asks you twice if you understand what you are surrendering to. “Better than you do,” you tell her, and watch the sentence land somewhere she'll be keeping it.`)):(""))+P(`They weigh you. They measure your realm with a jade plate that fogs and cracks — the intake clerk notes, unblinking: <i>meridians sealed, external weaver, gold-aspect, UNPRECEDENTED, see Lady's page</i>. They tag your wrist with white silk, and the tag's knot is the first Court weaving you've seen up close: clean, dense, loveless, and very good. And they walk you through the intake hall, past the ledger of souls — a wall of reels, every consignment in the watershed for four centuries, each one a wound thread no thicker than a hair, each one a person, racked and indexed and DUSTED, because the Court does not neglect what it owns.`)+((G.f.a3_marked=="sho")?(P(`Somewhere above, in the guest terraces, an old woman with a claimed shoulder is being honored within an inch of her patience. The thought is a porch light. You walk toward it.`)):(P(`Somewhere above, in the guest terraces, a bookkeeper with a claimed shoulder is being honored within an inch of his ledger. The thought steadies you better than courage would.`))),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`The inner water-gate, and the city beyond it.`,go:"a4c21_city"}]};

SC["a4c21_city"]={img:"court",
 t:()=>P(`The Thousand Reels takes the breath you were saving.`)+P(`A city built ON the lake, not beside it: white pavilions on black pilings ringing a center of water, and across that center, everywhere, at every height, SILK — bridges of it, galleries of it, warp-lines running pavilion to pavilion like a harbor's rigging spun from cloud. Ten thousand reels turn slowly in the towers, paying out and winding in, and the whole city breathes with them: a tide of thread, in and out, regular as a sleeping chest. The evening sun comes through it all sideways and the air itself goes to gauze, and for one unguarded heartbeat you forget what the silk is for, because it is the most beautiful thing you have seen in two worlds.`)+P(`Then your eyes adjust, the basement's old training sorting wonder into loads, and you see what the rigging hangs FROM: every line in the city, every bridge, every breathing reel, runs down through the water and tightens toward something beneath the lake. The city isn't a city that contains a loom. The city is the loom's topside. The Thousand Reels is a machine for holding something shut, and ten thousand people live on the knuckles of its fist.`)+((G.f.a4_route=="guest")?(P(`“You looked up,” Madam Xian says, beside you at the rail, and her satisfaction is unfeigned. “The Lady will be pleased. Your quarters face the center, weaver. Most guests ask to be moved within the week. I have wagered tea that you won't.”`)):(""))+((G.f.a4_route=="spy")?(P(`“First time at the Reels?” says a tribute-clerk at the rail beside you, friendly, taking your stillness for a merchant's awe. “It does that. You stop seeing it after a season.” Wen Duo agrees aloud that a man could stop seeing anything, given a season, and files the sentence under everything that is wrong with this place.`)):(""))+((G.f.a4_route=="prisoner")?(P(`They let consignments see it. That's the detail you'll carry: the transfer barge pauses at the inner gate, deliberately, so the cargo can look UP — some last mercy or first sermon, you can't tell which. The guard at your elbow says, not unkindly, “Welcome to the warp,” and the tag on your wrist hums once, softly, finding its home current.`)):("")),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`In, along the white water-lanes, to whatever room the Court has chosen for you.`,go:"a4c21_quarters"}]};

SC["a4c21_quarters"]={t:()=>((G.f.a4_route=="guest")?(P(`Guest quarters: a pavilion of your own on the third ring, silk-screened, lake-floored, beautiful past argument. Mei, if asked, would note that every sightline in it is also a sightline INTO it; Ruan, unasked, measures the walls and writes one word in his book: <i>nine</i>. Nine separate threads run out of your rooms toward the towers. The Court listens with architecture.`)):(""))+((G.f.a4_route=="spy")?(P(`Wen Duo takes a trade-house room on the second ring, lake-cold floor, paper walls, perfect. By the first midnight you've mapped the four threads woven into its beams and learned to talk under them, by the second you've stood three drinks for the consignment schedulers, and by the third you hold a thing no guest is ever given: the WORKING calendar of the Grand Loom — feeding days, rest days, and a one-line entry repeating each month for forty years: <i>warp-elder W.S., continuous.</i>`)):(""))+((G.f.a4_route=="prisoner")?(P(`The holding pavilion is the kindest prison ever built: warm, clean, silk-screened, eight other consignments sleeping their fattened sleep around you. You alone are awake, untagged in every way that matters, reading the room's weave by lamplight. The guards check the silk tags, never the people. Your tag lies to them every hour on the hour, a small gold forgery riding inside its white knot, and meanwhile the pavilion's threads tell you everything: feeding schedules, duty rotations, and a current, steady as a heartbeat, running from beneath the lake up through every line in the city. The Loom is two doors away. You came in through the cargo entrance of the Court's whole religion.`)):(""))+((G.f.a3_mei_present)?(P(`Mei established herself in the guest infirmary within a day of landing — the Court, to her visible disgust, has excellent physicians and better records. “Their burn ward is forty years of the same burn,” she tells you at the first chance, low. “Thread-side scald, palm and wrist. The warp does it. They treat their own weavers like kiln-girls.” She has begun, without asking anyone, treating the kiln-girls.`)):(""))+SYS(`Route established. Tomorrow the Court keeps its oldest promise: the consignment your blind friend mourns. The audience is granted — Wen Suyin, warp-elder, forty years continuous.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Sleep, if the city's breathing lets you.`,go:"a4c22_call"}]};